{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbbFJLeVPkqbqw4SpGEL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate, a deliberately simple and high-variance model called `gist_typicality_class_size`. It passed the self-check, but the smoke fit puts it far behind the current best, so it will very likely be pruned.\n\n**Hypothesis.** People notice only a sequence's \"gist\": how many heads it has and how many runs (stretches of identical flips) it breaks into. A sequence looks random to the extent that many other same-length sequences share that gist. Moderate balance with moderate switching is a common gist and looks random. Rare gists look designed: one solid streak, strict alternation, or all heads then all tails. People pick the sequence with the more common gist, each with their own decisiveness, and guess on some trials at their own lapse rate.\n\n**How it's built.**\n- The one feature is the difference between the two sequences in the log of how many sequences share each one's gist. `compute_features` counts these exactly.\n- Decisiveness and lapse rate are per-person, drawn from population distributions with 400 slots (participant ids currently go up to 77).\n- This doesn't reuse the alternation-rate, balance or streak terms that every recent leading model builds on. Nothing in the existing or tried lists works this way.\n\n**Self-check.** `check_candidate` printed `OK`. On the 100-draw, single-chain smoke fit:\n- **Fit:** ELPD-LOO was about -3151, roughly 880 nats worse than the current best (`run_length_variety_preference`, -2272.9).\n- **Reliability:** PSIS-LOO was flagged unreliable, with 2.9% of trials having a high Pareto k against a 1% tolerance. The full fit may or may not clear that.\n- **Not checked:** convergence can't be verified with one chain. Novelty against the other models isn't covered by the check.\n\n**Critique.** It doesn't target the critique's one flagged discrepancy: p